{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ta1Lgak8qPfdycgAwe3mqj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd108-vdir\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/vdir: List Directory Contents Verbosely\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  vdir is a GNU coreutils utility equivalent to \"ls -l -b\". It lists directory contents in\n6\t  long format with non-printable characters escaped using C-style backslash sequences.\n7\t  macOS does not ship a vdir command; the Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n8\t  reference binary (gvdir, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n9\t  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\t  vdir shares the bulk of its logic with cmd/ls (srd008-ls). The implementation must invoke\n12\t  the same listing engine with hardcoded defaults for long format (-l) and C-style escaping\n13\t  (-b). vdir requires pkg/sys for SIGPIPE handling and extended file metadata.\n14\t\n15\tgoals:\n16\t  - G1: List directory contents in long format with C-style escaping of non-printable characters, matching GNU vdir (ls -l -b) output.\n17\t  - G2: Accept the same arguments as ls, with the only difference being the default format and quoting style.\n18\t\n19\trequirements:\n20\t  R1:\n21\t    title: Default behavior and output format\n22\t    items:\n23\t      - R1.1:\n24\t          text: |\n25\t            Must list directory contents in long format (-l) by default, regardless of\n26\t            whether stdout is a TTY. This matches GNU vdir behavior where -l is the default\n27\t            format. Long format fields are: permissions (10 chars), nlink, owner, group, size,\n28\t            mtime, name — matching the layout specified in srd008-ls R1.6 through R1.10.\n29\t      - R1.2:\n30\t          text: |\n31\t            Must escape non-printable characters in filenames using C-style backslash\n32\t            sequences by default. This matches the -b (--escape) behavior of ls. Backslash,\n33\t            newline, tab, and other control characters are printed as \\\\, \\n, \\t, and \\NNN\n34\t            (octal) respectively. Spaces in filenames are printed as \\  (backslash space).\n35\t      - R1.3:\n36\t          text: |\n37\t            Must print a \"total N\" block count line before the directory listing, where\n38\t            N = sum(fi.Blocks for all listed entries) / 2. This matches the long-format\n39\t            total line behavior specified in srd008-ls R1.10.\n40\t      - R1.4:\n41\t          text: |\n42\t            Must sort entries in the C locale order (LC_COLLATE=C) by default. Entries whose\n43\t            names start with \".\" are excluded unless -a or -A is given.\n44\t      - R1.5:\n45\t          text: When no directory arguments are given, must default to the current directory (\".\").\n46\t      - R1.6:\n47\t          text: Must accept all flags that ls accepts. vdir is identical to ls except for the default format (-l) and default quoting style (-b). All other behavior is inherited from ls.\n48\t\n49\t  R2:\n50\t    title: Exit codes and signal handling\n51\t    items:\n52\t      - R2.1:\n53\t          text: Must exit 0 when all listed paths are accessed and output is written successfully.\n54\t      - R2.2:\n55\t          text: Must exit 1 when a minor problem occurs (permission denied, file not found). Must print a diagnostic to stderr and continue processing remaining entries.\n56\t      - R2.3:\n57\t          text: Must exit 2 when a serious problem occurs such as an invalid command-line option, matching GNU vdir (and ls) exit-code contract.\n58\t      - R2.4:\n59\t          text: Must install a SIGPIPE handler at startup by calling pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() so that piping vdir output to head or other truncating consumers does not produce a broken-pipe error message.\n60\t\n61\tnon_goals:\n62\t  - vdir does not add any flags beyond what ls provides; it is strictly ls with different defaults.\n63\t  - Color output (--color) is not enabled by default in vdir; it must be explicitly requested.\n64\t  - Multi-column format (-C) is not the default; -l is the default.\n65\t  - Recursive listing (-R) is supported but not default behavior.\n66\t\n67\tacceptance_criteria:\n68\t  - id: AC1\n69\t    criterion: \"Default mode comparison -- gvdir and go run ./cmd/vdir on a test directory produce identical long-format output with escaped filenames. Differential tests must set LC_ALL=C.\"\n70\t    traces:\n71\t      - R1.1\n72\t      - R1.2\n73\t      - R1.3\n74\t      - R1.4\n75\t      - R1.5\n76\t      - R1.6\n77\t  - id: AC2\n78\t    criterion: \"Total line -- gvdir and go run ./cmd/vdir produce identical 'total N' block count lines.\"\n79\t    traces:\n80\t      - R1.3\n81\t  - id: AC3\n82\t    criterion: \"Escaping -- filenames containing spaces, backslashes, newlines, and control characters are escaped identically by gvdir and the Go binary.\"\n83\t    traces:\n84\t      - R1.2\n85\t  - id: AC4\n86\t    criterion: \"Exit codes -- the Go binary exits 1 when given a non-existent path and exits 2 for an invalid option, matching gvdir behavior.\"\n87\t    traces:\n88\t      - R2.1\n89\t      - R2.2\n90\t      - R2.3\n91\t      - R2.4\n92\t  - id: AC5\n93\t    criterion: \"cmd/vdir compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n94\t    traces:\n95\t      - R1.1\n96\t      - R1.2\n97\t      - R1.3\n98\t      - R1.4\n99\t      - R1.5\n100\t      - R1.6\n101\t      - R2.1\n102\t      - R2.2\n103\t      - R2.3\n104\t      - R2.4\n105\t\n106\tpackage_contract:\n107\t  imports:\n108\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/format\n109\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n110\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1d392bd-5d4d-4f03-9f3e-6208317b53d5","uuid":"96998aaa-60ae-4ea5-9596-dcbed921b08e","timestamp":"2026-05-27T21:32:39.765Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5618/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd108-vdir.yaml","content":"id: srd108-vdir\ntitle: \"cmd/vdir: List Directory Contents Verbosely\"\n\nproblem: |\n  vdir is a GNU coreutils utility equivalent to \"ls -l -b\". It lists directory contents in\n  long format with non-printable characters escaped using C-style backslash sequences.\n  macOS does not ship a vdir command; the Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n  reference binary (gvdir, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\n  vdir shares the bulk of its logic with cmd/ls (srd008-ls). The implementation must invoke\n  the same listing engine with hardcoded defaults for long format (-l) and C-style escaping\n  (-b). vdir requires pkg/sys for SIGPIPE handling and extended file metadata.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: List directory contents in long format with C-style escaping of non-printable characters, matching GNU vdir (ls -l -b) output.\n  - G2: Accept the same arguments as ls, with the only difference being the default format and quoting style.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior and output format\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: |\n            Must list directory contents in long format (-l) by default, regardless of\n            whether stdout is a TTY. This matches GNU vdir behavior where -l is the default\n            format. Long format fields are: permissions (10 chars), nlink, owner, group, size,\n            mtime, name — matching the layout specified in srd008-ls R1.6 through R1.10.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: |\n            Must escape non-printable characters in filenames using C-style backslash\n            sequences by default. This matches the -b (--escape) behavior of ls. Backslash,\n            newline, tab, and other control characters are printed as \\\\, \\n, \\t, and \\NNN\n            (octal) respectively. Spaces in filenames are printed as \\  (backslash space).\n      - R1.3:\n          text: |\n            Must print a \"total N\" block count line before the directory listing, where\n            N = sum(fi.Blocks for all listed entries) / 2. This matches the long-format\n            total line behavior specified in srd008-ls R1.10.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: |\n            Must sort entries in the C locale order (LC_COLLATE=C) by default. Entries whose\n            names start with \".\" are excluded unless -a or -A is given.\n      - R1.5:\n          text: When no directory arguments are given, must default to the current directory (\".\").\n      - R1.6:\n          text: Must accept all flags that ls accepts. vdir is identical to ls except for the default format (-l) and default quoting style (-b). All other behavior is inherited from ls.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes and signal handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all listed paths are accessed and output is written successfully.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when a minor problem occurs (permission denied, file not found). Must print a diagnostic to stderr and continue processing remaining entries.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must exit 2 when a serious problem occurs such as an invalid command-line option, matching GNU vdir (and ls) exit-code contract.\n      - R2.4:\n          text: Must install a SIGPIPE handler at startup by calling pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() so that piping vdir output to head or other truncating consumers does not produce a broken-pipe error message.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - vdir does not add any flags beyond what ls provides; it is strictly ls with different defaults.\n  - Color output (--color) is not enabled by default in vdir; it must be explicitly requested.\n  - Multi-column format (-C) is not the default; -l is the default.\n  - Recursive listing (-R) is supported but not default behavior.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"Default mode comparison -- gvdir and go run ./cmd/vdir on a test directory produce identical long-format output with escaped filenames. Differential tests must set LC_ALL=C.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"Total line -- gvdir and go run ./cmd/vdir produce identical 'total N' block count lines.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Escaping -- filenames containing spaces, backslashes, newlines, and control characters are escaped identically by gvdir and the Go binary.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Exit codes -- the Go binary exits 1 when given a non-existent path and exits 2 for an invalid option, matching gvdir behavior.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/vdir compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/format\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":110,"startLine":1,"totalLines":110}}}
