{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5618) to implement srd108-vdir requirements R2.3 and R2.4 in the go-unix-utils project. Specifically:\n   - R2.3: \"Must exit 2 when a serious problem occurs such as an invalid command-line option, matching GNU vdir (and ls) exit-code contract.\"\n   - R2.4: \"Must install a SIGPIPE handler at startup by calling pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() so that piping vdir output to head or other truncating consumers does not produce a broken-pipe error message.\"\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/vdir/main.go` (add implementation) and `cmd/vdir/vdir_test.go` (add differential test cases).\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: code compiles, go vet passes, tests pass (skip gracefully if gvdir not in PATH), each of R2.3 and R2.4 has at least one differential test case.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU reference binary (`gvdir`)\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Exit code 2 for invalid command-line options (GNU convention)\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for test parity\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for building test binaries\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gvdir\")` with `t.Skip` for graceful skip when reference binary absent\n   - `testutils.DiffTest` struct: `{Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles}`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd108-vdir.yaml`\n     - Read to understand R2.3 and R2.4 requirements\n     - R2.3: Exit 2 on invalid command-line option\n     - R2.4: Install SIGPIPE handler at startup\n   \n   - `cmd/vdir/main.go` (existing, 495 lines)\n     -