{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SLSHEPpSxGUYQeFxieQHdo","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have all the information you need. Here's a comprehensive summary of the differential testing structure using the `echo_test.go` as an example:\n\n## Echo Test Example - Full Differential Testing Structure\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5618/cmd/echo/echo_test.go`\n\nThis is an excellent example of differential testing because it:\n1. Tests a simple utility (echo)\n2. Uses the full testutils infrastructure\n3. Demonstrates exit code testing (both binaries expect exit 0)\n4. Shows comprehensive test case coverage with the DiffTest struct\n\n### Key Components:\n\n**Imports:**\n```go\nimport (\n    \"os/exec\"\n    \"testing\"\n    \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n```\n\n**BuildBinary Function:**\n- Compiles the Go package in the current directory (\".\")\n- Returns path to compiled binary\n- Cleans up automatically when test finishes\n- Fatals on build failure\n\n**RunDiffTests Function:**\n- Takes the Go binary path, reference binary path, and array of DiffTest structs\n- Executes each test as a named subtest\n- Compares stdout, stderr, and exit codes between Go implementation and reference (gecho)\n\n**DiffTest Struct Usage:**\nEach test case includes:\n- `Name`: Subtest name (e.g., \"no-args\", \"n-flag\")\n- `Args`: Command-line arguments (e.g., `[]string{\"-n\", \"hello\"}`)\n- `Stdin`: Standard input bytes (nil, empty slice, or actual bytes)\n- `Env`: Environment variables (LC_ALL=C applied by default)\n- `ExitCode`: Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n- `Normalize`: Optional output normalization functions\n- `WorkDir`: Working directory for test\n- `ExpectedFiles`: Map of expected file outputs\n\n**Exit Code Testing:**\nExit codes are automatically captured and compared between both binaries through the `binaryResult` struct in testutils, which extracts the exit code using `exec.ExitError.ExitCode()` when the command fails.\n\nThe test framework runs both binaries with identical inputs and compares:\n- stdout (byte-for-byte)\n- stderr (byte-for-byte)  \n- exit codes (integers)\n\nIf any mismatch occurs, it provides a detailed divergence report showing args, stdin, actual vs expected output, and actual vs expected exit codes."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1d392bd-5d4d-4f03-9f3e-6208317b53d5","uuid":"f0fb0541-36aa-489a-9a65-2c7052e3de50","timestamp":"2026-05-27T21:33:55.313Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5618, find a cmd/*_test.go file that uses testutils.RunDiffTests and testutils.BuildBinary for differential testing. Show me the full contents of one good example (preferably a simple utility like cat, echo, or yes). I need to see the test structure including imports, TestDiff function, DiffTest struct usage, and how exit codes are tested.","agentId":"a5f3ed241ccfd69b2","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have all the information you need. Here's a comprehensive summary of the differential testing structure using the `echo_test.go` as an example:\n\n## Echo Test Example - Full Differential Testing Structure\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5618/cmd/echo/echo_test.go`\n\nThis is an excellent example of differential testing because it:\n1. Tests a simple utility (echo)\n2. Uses the full testutils infrastructure\n3. Demonstrates exit code testing (both binaries expect exit 0)\n4. Shows comprehensive test case coverage with the DiffTest struct\n\n### Key Components:\n\n**Imports:**\n```go\nimport (\n    \"os/exec\"\n    \"testing\"\n    \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n```\n\n**BuildBinary Function:**\n- Compiles the Go package in the current directory (\".\")\n- Returns path to compiled binary\n- Cleans up automatically when test finishes\n- Fatals on build failure\n\n**RunDiffTests Function:**\n- Takes the Go binary path, reference binary path, and array of DiffTest structs\n- Executes each test as a named subtest\n- Compares stdout, stderr, and exit codes between Go implementation and reference (gecho)\n\n**DiffTest Struct Usage:**\nEach test case includes:\n- `Name`: Subtest name (e.g., \"no-args\", \"n-flag\")\n- `Args`: Command-line arguments (e.g., `[]string{\"-n\", \"hello\"}`)\n- `Stdin`: Standard input bytes (nil, empty slice, or actual bytes)\n- `Env`: Environment variables (LC_ALL=C applied by default)\n- `ExitCode`: Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n- `Normalize`: Optional output normalization functions\n- `WorkDir`: Working directory for test\n- `ExpectedFiles`: Map of expected file outputs\n\n**Exit Code Testing:**\nExit codes are automatically captured and compared between both binaries through the `binaryResult` struct in testutils, which extracts the exit code using `exec.ExitError.ExitCode()` when the command fails.\n\nThe test framework runs both binaries with identical inputs and compares:\n- stdout (byte-for-byte)\n- stderr (byte-for-byte)  \n- exit codes (integers)\n\nIf any mismatch occurs, it provides a detailed divergence report showing args, stdin, actual vs expected output, and actual vs expected exit codes."}],"totalDurationMs":23023,"totalTokens":34217,"totalToolUseCount":7,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":618,"cache_read_input_tokens":32981,"output_tokens":613,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":618},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":613,"cache_read_input_tokens":32981,"cache_creation_input_tokens":618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":618,"ephemeral